{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785092248,"nonce":"c/P8TEdJUtGZilQWsipuk5yo8hc=","title":"Browse reports a symlink as a file and streams its target path as the file's contents","message":"Cosmetic, no correctness impact on execution — but it is a lie in the UI: open\na symlink in the run-detail Browse tab and you get a one-line \"file\" whose\ncontents are a path.\n\nVerified at `bd30a71`. Not part of any ADR-0061 slice; it is a consequence of\na deliberate s7 design choice.\n\n---\n\n\nADR-0061 s7 (`dd67e12`) gave symlinks **git's representation**: a symlink is a\n**blob holding the link target**, marked by `MODE_SYMLINK` in the tree entry's\n`mode` file-type bits (`crates/scarab-storage/src/lib.rs:39`, `:61`, `:91`).\n\nThat was chosen precisely so that nothing downstream needed to change: GC's\nmark walk still sees a blob and reaches it, `prune_tree` still works,\n`tree_entries` still returns two target kinds, and the browse API compiled\nunchanged. Not introducing a third `TreeTarget` variant was the point — the\nscoping decision for the `/flat` wire format repeats the same rule (\"Symlinks\nare entries whose `mode` file-type bits are `MODE_SYMLINK` — do **not** invent\na third variant\").\n\n\n`crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs:2796-2799` — the listing maps target kind to\na two-valued string and never consults the mode:\n\n```rust\nkind: match e.target {\n    TreeTarget::Tree(_) =\u003e \"dir\",\n    TreeTarget::Blob(_) =\u003e \"file\",\n}\n```\n\n`WorkspaceEntryDto` (`:2648-2653`) documents `kind` as `\"dir\"` (a sub-tree) or\n`\"file\"` (a blob) — accurate about the CAS, wrong about the filesystem the\nsnapshot represents. And `GET /v1/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/workspace/file`\nstreams the blob bytes, so fetching a symlink returns its **target path as\nfile content** with no indication that is what happened.\n\n\nThe question is already answered in the storage crate —\n`TreeEntry::is_symlink()` (`crates/scarab-storage/src/lib.rs:97-99`):\n\n```rust\npub fn is_symlink(\u0026self) -\u003e bool {\n    matches!(self.mode, Some(m) if m \u0026 MODE_TYPE_MASK == MODE_SYMLINK)\n}\n```\n\n- Emit `kind: \"symlink\"` from the listing, with the target as its own field\n  (read the blob — it is a path, so it is tiny; or defer the read and let the\n  UI fetch it).\n- Update the `WorkspaceEntryDto` doc comment (it is the OpenAPI source of\n  truth — tags/descriptions come from source in this repo) and regenerate\n  `openapi.gen.json`.\n- Render it as a link in the UI Browse tab\n  (`ui/scarab-web-ui/src/components/StepPane.tsx`), resolving within the\n  snapshot where the target is relative and in-tree, and showing it as a\n  dangling/absolute link otherwise. The existing sort (\"directories first,\n  then lexicographic\", `:2801`) needs a decision for the new kind — grouping\n  symlinks with files is fine.\n- Decide what `/workspace/file` does for a symlink: either 409/redirect with\n  the target, or keep streaming the bytes but set a header/field so the client\n  knows. Do not silently keep pretending it is a regular file.\n\n\nDo NOT change the CAS representation. Blob-with-`MODE_SYMLINK` is correct and\nis what keeps GC and pruning simple. This is purely an API/UI presentation\ngap.","files":null}]}